      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is because Android render bottom to top, while PC do top to bottom.\n\n(root of issue)\n\nTo avoid this bug permanentaly, but also to avoid flipping again when the bug is fixed, the colors of each pixel is obtained with Texture2D.GetPixels()\n\n, and only when an inversion is detected, Texture2D.SetPixels()\n\n and Texture2D.Apply()\n\n are used to flip the texture up or down.\n\nhttps://github.com/vr-lifemagazine/wall-newspaper-asset/commit/75eb13cefd7b7291b35f34e7a48c84add83ba542#diff-2e4dff698e5068f678f95b2c0ba644330c539fc84341e03223a2ac100489ba7e\n\nThis workaround, however, can only be used if a texture has areas that do not change color when updated and change color when flipped upside down.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
